    "created_at": "2020-04-22T03:22:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-22T03:22:31Z",
    "body": "I think we're in a better position to tackle this issue now, as:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5154 made explicit concepts for parser document and preparation-time document, which can be compared to each other and to the execution-time document.\r\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2673 added one mismatched document check that most everyone agreed on.\r\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/19632 added a framework for comprehensively testing cases of this sort.\r\n\r\nIn particular there are two pieces of the current spec that are signposted as \"under debate\":\r\n\r\n- [Prepare a script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#prepare-a-script) step 12 checks the parser document against the preparation-time document\r\n- [Execute a script block](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#execute-the-script-block) step 2 checks the parser document against the execution-time document.\r\n\r\n@hiroshige-g, would you be able to extend your test generator to see whether browsers implement these checks or not? That seems like the first step.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
