    "created_at": "2020-05-24T01:50:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-24T01:50:49Z",
    "body": "> @hiroshige-g, would you be able to extend your test generator to see whether browsers implement these checks or not? That seems like the first step.\r\n\r\nDoesn't the test generator already support testing the points scenarios you raised @domenic?\r\n - It looks like [here](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/moving-between-documents/resources/moving-between-documents-helper.js#L142-L147) we test that scripts are not executed when moved to a new document mid-parse\r\n    - The results can be seen [here](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/moving-between-documents?label=experimental&label=master&aligned), and it seems like Chrome is the only impl (I'm not counting Edge) that actually fails any before-prepare tests\r\n - I think the \"after-prepare\" tests also cover the execution-document checks as well, especially since  https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2673 cited https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/19632 as the relevant WPTs",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
